Subject: Transport original camera serialized words and native placement storage

Upstream-base: c7b2e663f878d38dc429ab12ee7db451daf0c217

Keep the original camera loading, owning/borrowed records, copying, list and
callback algorithms. Before the original direct word reads, ask the native
platform to convert completed Wii chunk headers and the consumed camera word
channels in place, retaining the original allocation and surrounding bytes.
NIS's original borrowed LoadAnimCameraData call uses the same representation.

The three original debug-camera placement requests retain alignment, direction,
constructor arguments and branch order; native backing uses sizeof(cDebugCamera)
because its LP64 footprint exceeds the retail 0xA0 physical storage request.

No original initialization, catalog, camera selection or playback is changed.
Platform byte domains require the reviewed allocation/completion metadata.
This does not establish original file request, camera runtime or scene startup.

